<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert E. Lee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1807">1807</a>–<a href="/years/1870">1870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Robert Edward Lee</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert E. Lee was an American soldier who commanded the Confederate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-northern-virginia">Army of Northern Virginia</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>. A Virginian and veteran of the Mexican–American War, he declined a senior Union command in 1861 and won major victories at the Seven Days, Second Manassas, Fredericksburg and Chancellorsville, but was defeated at Gettysburg in 1863. He surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a> at Appomattox Court House on 9 April 1865.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee.jpg" alt="Robert E. Lee" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian Vannerson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Edward_Lee_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
